          skills21stCentury: "Communication and Collaboration: Learners use talk for learning strategies to:\n● Build on each other's ideas by adding relevant related ideas to support/extend/refute the theme/s in narrative texts.\n● Convey simple ideas or thoughts to a wider group.\n● Engage the audience using different presentation techniques.\n\nLeadership Skills and Personal Development: Learners use the knowledge gained to:\n● Plan and organise activities confidently.\n● Organise allocated tasks between different team members.\n● Know when peers need support or assistance.\n● Take responsibility for their own learning.\n\nDigital Literacy Skills: Learners use ICT tools to:\n● Apply a variety of subject appropriate technologies to gather information on varied themes.\n● Prepare presentation slides.\n● Present their findings either in print or any appropriate medium of communication.\n\nCritical-thinking and Problem-solving skills: Learners think critically to:\n● Share ideas, ask questions and evaluate one another's ideas respectively.\n● Apply knowledge to real life situations by examining evidence in order to solve problems.\n\nCreativity and Innovation Skills: Learners use knowledge gained to:\n● Convey simple ideas of immediate interest to other persons in a team.\n● Generate multiple ideas when given initial ideas as a starting point.\n● Apply knowledge of theme and style to creatively explore prose texts and present information in an innovative way.\n\nCollaboration and Communication: Learners use the skills gained to:\n● Share ideas as they learn and build on each other's ideas.\n● Learn to understand, relate to and be sensitive to others.\n● Discuss using specific literacy and language of literature.\n● Communicate confidently and effectively to different participants/members in the group.\n\nCreativity and Innovation: learners use the knowledge and skills gained to:\n● Critique texts of different styles.\n● Explore prose texts and present the information in an innovative way.\n\nCritical-thinking and Problem-solving: Learners think critically to:\n● Question and understand the opinions and ideas of others to select the right information.\n● Analyse how technique is embedded in texts to bring out meaning.\n● Apply knowledge of the elements to explore the meaning of texts.",
